Native Fish source is pinned to 1ff3c3ed2f80d3106a83909dd25b83129c3d816f.
Its full LICENSE is retained at /opt/fish-speech/LICENSE in the image and in
FISH_LICENSE.txt in this mod. No weights are included in the image.

The Fish source is unchanged. Packaging uses PyTorch 2.13 and Torchaudio 2.11
CUDA 13 rather than upstream 2.8, and overrides Torchaudio's Torch 2.11 pin
and audiotools' obsolete protobuf constraint. The used Python resampler and
imports are qualified separately; general binary-extension parity is not claimed.
A separately authored MIT adapter bounds HTTP inputs, serializes native inference,
decodes bounded reference WAV using soundfile for Torchaudio 2.13 compatibility,
and exposes a small LAN-only evaluation UI. It does not change Fish model kernels.
Requests without an explicit reference use LJ Speech LJ001-0001, published as
public domain by Keith Ito and Linda Johnson (https://keithito.com/LJ-Speech-Dataset/).
Its immutable mirror/source revision and audio SHA-256 are in reference-provenance.json.
Unconditioned native synthesis failed full-text ASR qualification; the released
profile therefore uses this disclosed, checksum-pinned reference, not a claimed
qualified unconditioned/random default voice.

